# A road drawn with the Road button that ends on a node of another road is refused (the Road button holds no view flag
# bit 3, docs/rules/roads.md#the-pointer-button-that-places-a-flag-on-a-road): the click is ignored, the other road
# keeps its carrier, and no flag appears there. Run it on the game view with seed 1234567812345678 and size 1:
#   sh tools/play-run.sh road-on-road --game-view --seed 1234567812345678 --size 1 --fps 10
# The castle stands at 21,4, its flag at 22,5; the woodcutter's flag is at 27,5 and the road between them runs east. A
# flag at 25,7 starts the road that goes north to 25,6 and then onto 25,5, a node of that road.
expect seed = 1234567812345678
expect size = 1
wait 0.3
click-tile 21 4
wait 0.3
button Woodcutter
click-tile 26 4
button Woodcutter
wait 0.3
button Flag
click-tile 25 7
button Flag
wait 0.3
button Road
click-tile 22 5
click-tile 23 5
click-tile 24 5
click-tile 25 5
click-tile 26 5
click-tile 27 5
button Road
wait 0.3
fast-forward carrier state 0x42 max 20000
wait 0.3
expect-count road >= 4
expect-count flag = 3
shot before 25 6 3 3
list before

button Road
click-tile 25 7
click-tile 25 6
click-tile 25 5
wait 0.3
shot refused 25 6 3 3
list refused
expect-at 25 5 road
expect-count flag = 3
button Road
wait 0.3
wait 40
expect-count carrier >= 1
shot carrier 25 5 3 3
list after
dump after
